  "intro": "A random variable assigns a number to each outcome. A discrete random variable has a probability distribution listing values and probabilities that sum to $1$. Its mean (expected value) is $\\mu=E(X)=\\sum x_i\\,P(x_i)$, and its variance is $\\sigma^2=\\sum (x_i-\\mu)^2 P(x_i)$. Linear rules: $E(aX+b)=aE(X)+b$ and $\\text{Var}(aX+b)=a^2\\text{Var}(X)$. For independent $X,Y$: $E(X+Y)=E(X)+E(Y)$ and $\\text{Var}(X+Y)=\\text{Var}(X)+\\text{Var}(Y)$.",
  "items": [
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 1,
      "prompt": "A variable takes values $0,1,2$ with probabilities $0.2,0.5,0.3$. Find $E(X)$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Multiply each value by its probability: $0(0.2)+1(0.5)+2(0.3)$.",
          "Compute: $0+0.5+0.6=1.1$.",
          "So the expected value is $1.1$."
        ],
        "answer": "$E(X)=1.1$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 2,
      "prompt": "If $E(X)=5$, find $E(2X+3)$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Apply $E(aX+b)=aE(X)+b$.",
          "$2(5)+3=10+3=13$."
        ],
        "answer": "$13$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 3,
      "prompt": "If $\\text{Var}(X)=4$, find $\\text{Var}(3X)$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Use $\\text{Var}(aX)=a^2\\text{Var}(X)$.",
          "$3^2\\cdot 4=9\\cdot 4=36$."
        ],
        "answer": "$36$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "id": 4,
      "prompt": "$E(X)$ for values $1,2,3$ with probs $0.5,0.3,0.2$.",
